Article 1 The Shanghai Financial Court shall have jurisdiction over the following first-instance financial civil and commercial cases within the jurisdiction of Shanghai Municipality that shall be accepted by the Intermediate People's Court:
(1) financial civil and commercial disputes such as those involving securities, futures trading, business trust, insurance, negotiable instruments, letters of credit, independent guarantees, factoring, financial loan contracts, bank cards, financial leasing contracts, entrusted wealth management contracts, savings deposit contracts, pawnbroking, and bank settlement contracts;
(2) financial civil and commercial disputes arising from asset management business, asset-backed securities business, private equity fund business, foreign exchange business, financial product sales and suitability management, credit information business, payment business, and other financial businesses approved by the competent authority;
(3) company-related disputes involving financial institutions;
(4) bankruptcy disputes in which a financial institution is the debtor;
(5) judicial review cases of arbitration concerning financial civil and commercial disputes;
(6) cases applying for recognition and enforcement of judgments and rulings of the courts of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region, the Macao Special Administrative Region, and the Taiwan region concerning financial civil and commercial disputes, as well as cases applying for recognition and enforcement of judgments and rulings of foreign courts concerning financial civil and commercial disputes.

Article 2 The Shanghai Financial Court shall have jurisdiction over the following financial dispute cases:
(1) actions instituted with the Shanghai Financial Court by domestic investors on the grounds that securities issuance, trading activities, or futures trading activities occurring outside the territory of the People's Republic of China have harmed their lawful rights and interests;
(2) actions instituted with the Shanghai Financial Court by domestic individuals or institutions on the grounds that financial products sold or financial services provided by financial institutions outside the territory of the People's Republic of China have harmed their lawful rights and interests.
